1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,310
This is the implementation demo for journey eight.

2
00:00:03,310 --> 00:00:07,220
It is the real application and API running on this machine,

3
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:12,510
with synthetic people and the local payment adapter, so nothing is ever charged.

4
00:00:12,510 --> 00:00:16,490
It shows how a buyer adds a second car at the cheaper price.

5
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:23,060
A buyer who has already booked one car sees a banner on the dashboard: their window

6
00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:28,100
is open until a date two weeks out, and another car to compare is twenty five

7
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:28,620
dollars.

8
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:31,370
The add another car button opens a dialog.

9
00:00:31,370 --> 00:00:36,470
Continuing without a VIN puts focus on the VIN field and says what is missing.

10
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:39,080
Now the next car's VIN and both reviews.

11
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:42,680
The booking flow opens with that VIN already filled in,

12
00:00:42,680 --> 00:00:44,640
and the review already chosen.

13
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:49,480
The order shows forty five dollars: twenty five for an additional vehicle,

14
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,370
plus twenty for both reviews.

15
00:00:51,370 --> 00:00:54,250
The buyer picks a time, pays, and is booked.

16
00:00:54,250 --> 00:00:57,910
Back on the dashboard, a message says the car was added,

17
00:00:57,910 --> 00:01:00,530
and how many cars are now in the window.

18
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:04,730
The price is never worked out in the browser.

19
00:01:04,730 --> 00:01:10,420
A buyer who has not paid yet has no window, and a first inspection is fifty dollars.

20
00:01:10,420 --> 00:01:13,810
After the first payment the server opens a window.

21
00:01:13,810 --> 00:01:16,990
From then on another car quotes at twenty five.

22
00:01:16,990 --> 00:01:21,870
The window lasts fourteen days, and it is open up to, but not including,

23
00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:23,020
its last instant.

24
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:27,770
With two days or less left it warns, and the warning can be dismissed.

25
00:01:27,770 --> 00:01:33,460
Once it has closed, a new inspection is fifty dollars again and starts a new window.

26
00:01:33,460 --> 00:01:37,190
Cancelling or refunding a car never changes the window,

27
00:01:37,190 --> 00:01:39,350
but refunded cars stop counting.

28
00:01:39,350 --> 00:01:44,710
These rules are written down as an architecture decision, and covered by tests.

29
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:47,600
Here is what to remember.

30
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:51,020
A window is fourteen days from the first payment.

31
00:01:51,020 --> 00:01:56,180
Inside it another car is twenty five dollars, and both reviews add twenty.

32
00:01:56,180 --> 00:02:00,090
The server decides eligibility and price, so the banner,

33
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:02,950
the dialog and the checkout always agree.

34
00:02:02,950 --> 00:02:05,950
Next, journey nine: add a body shop review.
